msgstr "Me pēhea te whakamahi i tēnei whārangi"

#: packages/scaffold/src/i18n.json
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "cli.scaffold:scaffold.canvas-theme-editor.i18n.helpModalBody1"
msgid ""
"Pick a starter template, edit it like you would in the Canvas Rich Content "
"Editor, then click <strong>Copy HTML</strong> and paste the result into a "
"Canvas page (switch to the HTML editor view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted "
"HTML server-side — this preview doesn't attempt to replicate that, so always "
"verify the pasted result in Canvas."
msgstr ""
"Tīpakohia he tauira tīmatanga, whakatikahia pēnei i roto i te Kaiwhakatika "
"Ihirangi Rawa o Canvas, katahi ka pāwhiri <strong>Copy HTML</strong> ka "
"whakapiri te hua ki tētahi whārangi Canvas (hurihia ki te tirohanga "
"kaiwhakatika HTML i te tuatahi). Ka ārai a Canvas i te HTML i whakapirihia i "
"te taha tūmau — kāore tēnei matakitaki e kopa i tērā, nō reira me whakamātau "
"tonu i te hua kua whakapirihia i roto i Canvas."

#: packages/scaffold/src/i18n.json
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "cli.scaffold:scaffold.canvas-theme-editor.i18n.helpModalBody2"
msgid ""
"Use <strong>Edit theme</strong> to change the CDN provider, theme, or mode, "
"and to hand-edit the generated <code>theme.css</code>/<code>theme.js</code> "
"before downloading them."
msgstr ""
"Whakamahia te <strong>Edit theme</strong> ki te huri i te kaiwhakarato CDN, "
"te kaupapa, te aratau, me te āta whakatika i ngā kōnae whakauru "
"<code>theme.css</code>/<code>theme.js</code> i mua i te tikiake."

